# Checklist

- Is the component decomposition axis the right one (task / domain /
  workflow)? Flag forced or unnatural groupings.
- Do components have coherent responsibilities (one axis of work), or
  do they bundle unrelated concerns?
- Are the labeled techspec blocks each specific enough that a
  downstream tier can act on them? Flag thin or filler blocks.
- Does `<technologies>` faithfully record the concrete choices named
  in the input? Flag invented technologies or missing ones.
- Are cross-cutting concerns handled as policies or the foundation
  component, rather than duplicated across several components?
- Is the foundation component genuinely foundational, or a dumping
  ground?
- Does every policy declare exactly one of `<required>` or
  `<structural/>`, or neither — never both? Is a `<structural/>`
  policy genuinely structural, or does it actually reduce to one
  responsibility and belong on `<required>` instead?
- Is every responsibility assigned to exactly one component?
